AWS ECR & ECS Deployment
1. ECR — Push Docker Image

Flow:

Create ECR Repository
        ↓
View Push Commands
        ↓
Create IAM Role
        ↓
Give ECR Permissions
        ↓
Attach Role to EC2
        ↓
Login to EC2
        ↓
Execute Docker / ECR Commands
        ↓
Docker Image → ECR

Steps

Create ECR Repository

Create a repository for the application image.

View Push Commands

Open the repository → View push commands.

Create IAM Role

Create an IAM role with required ECR permissions.

Attach the role to the EC2 instance.

Push Image

Login to EC2.

Build the Docker image.

Authenticate Docker with ECR.

Tag the image.

Push the image to ECR.

Docker Image
     ↓
   Build
     ↓
   Tag
     ↓
   Push
     ↓
ECR Repository

2. ECS — Run Application

Flow:

ECS Cluster
    ↓
Task Definition
    ↓
Select ECR Image
    ↓
Create ECS Service
    ↓
Select Task Definition
    ↓
Select Fargate
    ↓
Set Desired Tasks / Replicas
    ↓
Configure VPC + Subnet + Security Group
    ↓
Create Service
    ↓
Running ECS Tasks

Steps

Create ECS Cluster

Create the ECS cluster.

Create Task Definition

Define how the container should run.

Select the ECR image.

Configure CPU, memory, container port, environment variables, etc.

Create Service

Select the cluster.

Select the task definition.

Select Fargate.

Set the required number of replicas/tasks.

Networking

Select VPC.

Select subnets.

Configure the security group.

Configure public/private networking as required.

Complete Flow
                    ECR
                     │
              Create Repository
                     ↓
              Build Docker Image
                     ↓
              Push Image to ECR
                     │
                     ↓
                    ECS
                     │
              Create Cluster
                     ↓
             Create Task Definition
                     ↓
              Select ECR Image
                     ↓
               Create Service
                     ↓
                 Fargate
                     ↓
              Set Replicas/Tasks
                     ↓
             Configure Networking
                     ↓
               Running Application

Key Difference
ECR     → Stores the Docker Image
ECS     → Manages the Container
Fargate → Runs the Container without managing EC2 servers
Task Definition → Tells ECS what/how to run
Service → Maintains the required number of Tasks
